      <item>
        <title>There&apos;s now an agent skill set available for dealing with this CVE. Helps you determine whether you were ever exposed to this issue, and making sure you&apos;re properly patched. Great use of AI! https://github.com/rails/rails-forensics-CVE-2026-66066</title>
        <dc:creator>@dhh</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>There's now an agent skill set available for dealing with this CVE. Helps you determine whether you were ever exposed to this issue, and making sure you're properly patched. Great use of AI! <a href="https://github.com/rails/rails-forensics-CVE-2026-66066">github.com/rails/rails-foren…</a></p>
<hr/>
<b>Link</b><br>
<a href="https://github.com/rails/rails-forensics-CVE-2026-66066">
<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/card_img%2F2082997688472330240%2FlgyBgTZg%3Fformat%3Djpg%26name%3D800x419" style="max-width:250px;" />
<br>
<b>GitHub - rails/rails-forensics-CVE-2026-66066</b>
</a>
<p>Contribute to rails/rails-forensics-CVE-2026-66066 development by creating an account on GitHub.</p>
<small><a href="https://github.com/rails/rails-forensics-CVE-2026-66066">github.com</a></small>

<hr/>
<blockquote>
<b>DHH (@dhh)</b>
<p>
<p>You need to upgrade your Rails application right away if you're using Active Storage to store files and allow uploads from untrusted users. The underlying libvips used for image processing has a severe security issue. Great work by <a href="https://nitter.net/flavorjones" title="mike dalessio">@flavorjones</a> to lead the response on this.</p>

</p>
<footer>
— <cite><a href="https://nitter.net/dhh/status/2082494001714782365#m">https://nitter.net/dhh/status/2082494001714782365#m</a>
</footer>
</blockquote>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:11:40 GMT</pubDate>
