      <item>
        <title>The second question is always: How do you deal with the glare!? Don&apos;t you have to keep the blinds down all day? And the answer is no, thanks to 3M and SCIENCE! Incredible technology. https://www.3m.com/3M/en_US/home-window-solutions-us/solutions/glare-reduction/</title>
        <dc:creator>@dhh</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>The second question is always: How do you deal with the glare!? Don't you have to keep the blinds down all day? And the answer is no, thanks to 3M and SCIENCE! Incredible technology. <a href="https://www.3m.com/3M/en_US/home-window-solutions-us/solutions/glare-reduction/">3m.com/3M/en_US/home-window-…</a></p>
<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/media%2FHOe64PuXcAAXC4B.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />

<hr/>
<blockquote>
<b>David Senra (@davidsenra)</b>
<p>
<p>A picture of <a href="https://nitter.net/DHH" title="DHH">@DHH</a>'s desk goes viral every few months, and he says the number one comment he always gets is that it can't be a real office because it’s too clean.<br>
<br>
His response:<br>
<br>
"If I have shit all over my desk, I'm not creating work, because my mind will just go to the shit."<br>
<br>
“It's a bit like that Marie Kondo thing where you go through simplifying your home and throwing out all this stuff. It actually creates free mental space.”<br>
<br>
“I need this pure cocoon.”<br>
<br>
“It's actually a form of procrastination, and I need to run out of obvious things to procrastinate on before I'll start the real work.”</p>
<a href="https://nitter.net/davidsenra/status/2082261263963537428#m">
<br>Video<br>
  <img src="https://nitter.net/pic/amplify_video_thumb%2F2082261066579636224%2Fimg%2FUTeDBmMY9ueSYhzA.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />
</a>


</p>
<footer>
— <cite><a href="https://nitter.net/davidsenra/status/2082261263963537428#m">https://nitter.net/davidsenra/status/2082261263963537428#m</a>
</footer>
</blockquote>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:43:39 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082839544290820367</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/dhh/status/2082839544290820367#m</link>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Been using this three-way combo a lot lately. Great way to control a whole fleet of machines too. Every server is a tab, very easy to hop between them. Really well done.</title>
        <dc:creator>@dhh</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>Been using this three-way combo a lot lately. Great way to control a whole fleet of machines too. Every server is a tab, very easy to hop between them. Really well done.</p>
<hr/>
<blockquote>
<b>Termius (@TermiusHQ)</b>
<p>
<p>Termius + Tailscale + tmux<br>
<br>
You don't need your laptop to build with Claude Code, Codex, or any other AI coding agent:<br>
<br>
→ Run your agent inside tmux to keep the session alive<br>
→ Use <a href="https://nitter.net/Tailscale" title="Tailscale">@Tailscale</a> for secure access to your laptop<br>
→ Connect with Termius over SSH from iPhone, iPad, or Android<br>
<br>
Start coding at your desk. Continue on the go.</p>
<a href="https://nitter.net/TermiusHQ/status/2082616764605874207#m">
<br>Video<br>
  <img src="https://nitter.net/pic/amplify_video_thumb%2F2082616439052369920%2Fimg%2FwkBeC1Mc0xW4pj2y.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />
</a>


</p>
<footer>
— <cite><a href="https://nitter.net/TermiusHQ/status/2082616764605874207#m">https://nitter.net/TermiusHQ/status/2082616764605874207#m</a>
</footer>
</blockquote>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:03:02 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082829325212983297</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/dhh/status/2082829325212983297#m</link>
      </item>
