      <item>
        <title>R to @dhh: Free speech is critical to a high-functioning society. You can&apos;t just &quot;TrUST tHe SCiEnCe&quot;. Because some times &quot;science&quot; — aka the current consensus view — is just wrong! The way we correct it is by allowing critique and dissent. Science as a process, not a dogma.</title>
        <dc:creator>@dhh</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>Free speech is critical to a high-functioning society. You can't just "TrUST tHe SCiEnCe". Because some times "science" — aka the current consensus view — is just wrong! The way we correct it is by allowing critique and dissent. Science as a process, not a dogma.</p>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 21:07:23 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082573725682000312</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/dhh/status/2082573725682000312#m</link>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Using Basecamp to coordinate with agents makes the work visible to the whole team. Great for letting your most AI-forward developers show the rest of the team just how deep the rabbit hole goes. That&apos;s what @jorgemanru is doing wiht Marie Chef 👌</title>
        <dc:creator>@dhh</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>Using Basecamp to coordinate with agents makes the work visible to the whole team. Great for letting your most AI-forward developers show the rest of the team just how deep the rabbit hole goes. That's what <a href="https://nitter.net/jorgemanru" title="Jorge Manrubia">@jorgemanru</a> is doing wiht Marie Chef 👌</p>
<hr/>
<blockquote>
<b>Jason Fried (@jasonfried)</b>
<p>
<p>Agent Marie has been busy in our Basecamp today. Adding cards, commenting on replies, writing up reports, digging into stubborn issues, fixing bugs, preparing PRs.<br>
<br>
Everything posted right to Basecamp, just as if Marie was a human, so other humans (and agents) can follow along and get involved.<br>
<br>
No special AI features in Basecamp, no AI-is-always-in-the-way overload. Just invite your own agents in, point them at the Basecamp CLI, and they'll get to work just like your own human crew.</p>
<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/media%2FHOan9zvWMAAnIyv.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />

<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/media%2FHOapsN_X0AAMjXc.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />


</p>
<footer>
— <cite><a href="https://nitter.net/jasonfried/status/2082538783925235850#m">https://nitter.net/jasonfried/status/2082538783925235850#m</a>
</footer>
</blockquote>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 20:21:35 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082562200019857652</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/dhh/status/2082562200019857652#m</link>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>You need to upgrade your Rails application right away if you&apos;re using Active Storage to store files and allow uploads from untrusted users. The underlying libvips used for image processing has a severe security issue. Great work by @flavorjones to lead the response on this.</title>
        <dc:creator>@dhh</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>You need to upgrade your Rails application right away if you're using Active Storage to store files and allow uploads from untrusted users. The underlying libvips used for image processing has a severe security issue. Great work by <a href="https://nitter.net/flavorjones" title="mike dalessio">@flavorjones</a> to lead the response on this.</p>
<hr/>
<blockquote>
<b>Ruby on Rails (@rails)</b>
<p>
<p>We released new security versions of Rails to address a critical security bug in Active Storage. Please upgrade your applications.<br>
<br>
See the advisory for more information <a href="https://discuss.rubyonrails.org/t/cve-2026-66066-possible-arbitrary-file-read-and-remote-code-execution-in-active-storage-variant-processing/91432">discuss.rubyonrails.org/t/cv…</a></p>
<hr/>
<b>Link</b><br>
<a href="https://discuss.rubyonrails.org/t/cve-2026-66066-possible-arbitrary-file-read-and-remote-code-execution-in-active-storage-variant-processing/91432">
<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/card_img%2F2082256197864816641%2FTrr9FNRg%3Fformat%3Dpng%26name%3D420x420_2" style="max-width:250px;" />
<br>
<b>[CVE-2026-66066] Possible arbitrary file read and remote code execution in Active Storage variant...</b>
</a>
<p>See Possible arbitrary file read and remote code execution in Active Storage variant processing · Advisory · rails/rails · GitHub Impact In its default configuration, a Rails application that...</p>
<small><a href="https://discuss.rubyonrails.org/t/cve-2026-66066-possible-arbitrary-file-read-and-remote-code-execution-in-active-storage-variant-processing/91432">discuss.rubyonrails.org</a></small>


</p>
<footer>
— <cite><a href="https://nitter.net/rails/status/2082491600844816886#m">https://nitter.net/rails/status/2082491600844816886#m</a>
</footer>
</blockquote>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:50:35 GMT</pubDate>
